      "postID": "5a355aaf6949fa4b48fc2807",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "I recently got a HTC Vive and a new RX 580 and played for days with my old i5-4460 for days with no problems. Then I decided to upgrade my computer and got new everything including a new AMD cpu and then this problem happened. I installed old drivers for RX 580 off of a CD, I would have assumed it would have updated online though. This time I did not install through CD so for sure have most current version. It's either a problem with the processor or graphics drives, and it's probably drives as someone else pointed out. I'll have to test downgrading to an older version tomorrow.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
